      "side": 1,
      "message": "A few architectural and reproducibility points on `INSTALL_PACKAGES_LIST`:\n\n1. **Pinning versions instead of `\"latest\"`**: Using `package_version\u003d\"latest\"` means any future upload to CIPD can silently change or break builds across `ec-legacy` and release branches without a commit. Please pin explicit version tags/hashes (or read pinned versions from config).\n2. **Using existing CrOS SDK standalone toolchains (`b/522844685`) instead of custom `clang`/`gcc` subtools**:\n   - The CrOS SDK builder (`cros_setup_toolchains.py --create-packages`) already builds and publishes standalone, `lddtree`-wrapped toolchain tarballs containing Clang/LLVM, the real `sysroot_wrapper`, `compiler-rt` baremetal builtins (`libclang_rt.builtins-{armv7m,armv6m,riscv32}.a`), `newlib`/`glibc`, `libcxx`, `libunwind`, and `binutils` to `gs://chromiumos-sdk/\u003cTC_PATH\u003e` (`armv7m-cros-eabi`, `arm-none-eabi`, `riscv32-cros-elf`, and `x86_64-cros-linux-gnu`), with the verified version pinned in `chromiumos-overlay/chromeos/binhost/host/sdk_version.conf`.\n   - Following the same pattern as `util/coreboot_sdk.py` (which reads `coreboot-sdk-ec-dependencies.eclass` and downloads into `~/.cache/`), we can read `sdk_version.conf` and pull those official standalone toolchain tarballs rather than maintaining hand-written compiler wrappers in `chromiumos-overlay`.\n3. **`openssl` package**: `experimental/pbusse_at_google.com/chromiumos/infra/tools/openssl` is not defined in `crrev.com/c/8566017`. Also note that EC host utilities query `pkg-config --cflags --libs libcrypto` (in addition to `openssl`), so if we use `infra/3pp/static_libs/openssl/linux-amd64` (or a subtool), make sure `libcrypto.pc` is present.",
